<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Book of Chilam Balam of Maní</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Book of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/books-of-chilam-balam">Chilam Balam</a> of Maní is one of the Books of Chilam Balam, colonial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> written in the Yucatec Maya language with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> alphabet. Kept by the Xiu lineage of Maní in Yucatán, it contains prophecies, chronicles organised by the katun cycles of the Maya calendar, and medical and calendrical lore. It survives mainly through a 19th-century copy in the Códice Pérez.</p></div>
